{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"anatomy-of-a-game.png"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Declarations are stored properties","anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of the game type:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you construct the world with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"type":"text","text":" and collects every "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global"},{"type":"text","text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"cloak\""},{"type":"text","text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle is for — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"type":"text","text":".)"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"One value, two roles","anchor":"One-value-two-roles"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A declaration and a live reference are the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Written in the game body it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on all consult the current turn."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This works because each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID"},{"type":"text","text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References are always compile-checked. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.after(.take)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hook.holds(cloak)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer.north(bar)"},{"type":"text","text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Scenery","anchor":"Scenery"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every noun a room description names should answer when the player examines it. Declare a fixture with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let wall = Item.scenery(","    \"stone wall\", adjectives: \"rough\", synonyms: \"masonry\", \"old brickwork\",","    description: \"Mortar fills the cracks.\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This creates an ordinary "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" with a name, vocabulary, examine text, and the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/scenery"},{"type":"text","text":" trait. The fixture cannot be taken and gets no stock room-listing sentence. The name and synonyms contribute nouns and adjectives through the usual parser rules: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stone wall"},{"type":"text","text":" answers to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wall"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stone wall"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"old brickwork"},{"type":"text","text":" adds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"brickwork"},{"type":"text","text":" and the adjective "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"old"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives:"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synonyms:"},{"type":"text","text":" are variadic, so they read the way "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/synonyms(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" read inside an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Item { }"},{"type":"text","text":" block — one phrase per argument, no brackets. A synonym is a noun phrase, not a single word, which is why "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"old brickwork"},{"type":"text","text":" above counts as one argument."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A phrase that ends in one of the item’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nouns"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a name, and names are matched first. A phrase that doesn’t — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x rough"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take velvet"},{"type":"text","text":" — is a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"description"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and the parser answers one when it picks out exactly one thing in view and asks "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Which do you mean…?”"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when it picks out several. Second pass, always: a description can never take a phrase away from something that already answered to it as a name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Store it on your game or content bundle and place it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":", just like any other item:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    player.starts(in: hall)","    wall.starts(in: hall)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All arguments after the name are optional. Use the trailing trait block when scenery has another role:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let niche = Item.scenery(\"shadowed niche\", synonyms: \"alcove\") {","    container","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The niche can hold things and take item rules. For text that turns on the niche’s own state — open or shut, lit or dark — omit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"description:"},{"type":"text","text":" and put "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"description(when: \\.isOpen, …, otherwise: …)"},{"type":"text","text":" in the trait block; for text that depends on anything else, attach a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"niche.describe { … }"},{"type":"text","text":" rule. Without any description, examining it uses the game’s stock examine line. Placement determines where a piece of scenery is visible, just as it does for other items."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol","anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"intro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tagline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the banner and scoring metadata.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — geography and initial placement, as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — all game logic, as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" value. Defaults to empty.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[SyntaxRule]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"noiseWords"},{"type":"text","text":" — filler words the parser drops from input before matching, beside the built-in articles, as "},{"code":"[String]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A spell game adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"spell\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses as ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Defaults to empty; a noise word that is also a verb, preposition or item word is a fatal diagnostic, since stripping it would make the word untypeable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what ","type":"text"},{"code":"X ME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" examines).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The `map` block","anchor":"The-map-block"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" is a result-builder property that yields a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap"},{"type":"text","text":" — a flat list of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry"},{"type":"text","text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" covers all of them."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"definition"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" is everything that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entire mutable state is a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.isWorn"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.score += 1"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"See also","anchor":"See-also"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Anatomy of a Game"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/scenery":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The item is part of the scenery: it cannot be taken, and it never earns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stock listing sentence — on the floor, on a surface, or inside a container"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alike. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firstSight"},{"type":"text","text":" text, if any, still appears; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scenery"},{"type":"text","text":" withholds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"engine’s line, never the author’s."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/scenery","title":"scenery","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"scenery"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ItemTrait"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/scenery","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"anatomy-of-a-game.png":{"type":"image","alt":"An open book becomes a cutaway house with connected rooms and a staircase.","identifier":"anatomy-of-a-game.png","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/Gnusto\/anatomy-of-a-game.png","traits":["1x","light"]}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Command":{"abstract":[{"text":"A parsed player command, available inside rule bodies as ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Command","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/command","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Command"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Command"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/World":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"title":"World","abstract":[{"text":"Rules that apply everywhere, declared through the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"text":" identifier in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"text":" block:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/world","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/name":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","title":"name","abstract":[{"text":"The item’s display name.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"name","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/name","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","title":"scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Declares named scenery that the player can examine but cannot take.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"scenery"},{"k